Package: captiond
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pipewire
Suggests: kaption | qaption, ffmpeg
Description: local live speech captions from PipeWire audio
 Captiond recognizes speech in the computer's audio and, separately, an
 explicitly selected microphone using local Whisper models. It exposes
 captions through a Unix socket and a D-Bus interface. No model is included.
 .
 This package contains the daemon and the captionctl command-line client.
 Its user service and socket are installed without enabling them.

Package: libcaptiond-client0
Section: libs
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: client library for the captiond live caption service
 This library implements captiond's Unix socket protocol without a graphical
 toolkit. It lets applications receive captions and control recognition.

Package: libcaptiond-client-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libcaptiond-client0 (= ${binary:Version}), nlohmann-json3-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: development files for the captiond client library
 Headers, the linker symlink and CMake targets for building captiond clients.

Package: libcaptiond-client-tests-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libcaptiond-client-dev (= ${binary:Version}), captiond (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: captiond client testing helpers and speech fixtures
 The upstream stand-in daemon, private PipeWire test helpers and speech
 recordings support client tests without loading a recognition model.
